\caption(Each arrow represents one entire two-time hidden path, and its label is that path’s joint mass with both observations. Conditioning on the future symbol raises the first-time state1 marginal from0.1 to about0.24026.)
\alttext(A native two-column state trellis labels the four joint masses0.036,0.081,0.001 and0.036. Their sum is0.154, and future evidence changes the first state-one probability.)

> Reuse prefix and suffix sums

A discrete model has initial probabilities pi_i, transitions A_ij from state i to j,
and emissions B_i,k. Conditional on the current state, the next state follows A;
conditional on each state, its observation follows B. For fixed model parameters,
write alpha_t(i)=P(o_0..o_t,q_t=i) and beta_t(i)=P(o_(t+1)..o_(T−1) given q_t=i).
Grouping the joint path sum by its boundary state gives

$$
\alpha_0(i)=\pi_i B_{i,o_0},\qquad
\alpha_{t+1}(j)=B_{j,o_{t+1}}\sum_i\alpha_t(i)A_{ij},
$$
\alttext(The forward variable sums all prefix paths ending in each state, then multiplies by the next emission probability.)

$$
\beta_{T-1}(i)=1,\qquad
\beta_t(i)=\sum_j A_{ij}B_{j,o_{t+1}}\beta_{t+1}(j),\qquad
\gamma_t(i)=\frac{\alpha_t(i)\beta_t(i)}{\sum_j\alpha_t(j)\beta_t(j)}.
$$
\alttext(The backward variable sums future paths from each current state; multiplying prefix and suffix evidence and normalizing gives the smoothed state marginal.)

The likelihood is the sum of the last unscaled forward row. Filtering conditions on
the observed prefix; smoothing conditions on the whole sequence. The tiny example
therefore changes its first-time belief when the later symbol is revealed, while its
last filtered and smoothed marginals agree up to rounding.

Rabiner's [A tutorial on hidden Markov models and selected applications in speech
recognition](https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~murphyk/Software/HMM/rabiner.pdf),
Proceedings of the IEEE77(2),257–286(1989),
[doi:10.1109/5.18626](https://doi.org/10.1109/5.18626), develops the path sum,
forward/backward recursions and marginal-state criterion in SectionIII. SectionV.A
explains scaling and log evidence. The notation here uses zero-based time and state IDs.

> The library's precise scaling convention

Before normalizing forward row t, let z_t be its sum and c_t=1/z_t. The scaled
forward row a_t has sum approximately one and is the filtering distribution. It
satisfies a_t=(product of c_0 through c_t) times the unscaled alpha_t. The native
backward table b uses terminal b_(T−1)=c_(T−1) and multiplies its recurrence by c_t.
Thus b_t=(product of c_t through c_(T−1)) times the unscaled beta_t. Consequently,
in exact arithmetic for positive evidence,

$$
\sum_i a_t(i)b_t(i)=c_t,\qquad
\gamma_t(i)=\frac{a_t(i)b_t(i)}{\sum_j a_t(j)b_t(j)},\qquad
\log P(O)=-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log c_t.
$$
\alttext(The scaled forward-backward product sums to the current reciprocal scale, not necessarily one. Normalizing it gives state marginals, and negative log scales sum to log evidence.)

The backward rows are not probability distributions and can contain values larger
than one. The first table checks the product sum against c_t rather than assuming
unit normalization. Equivalent backward scaling conventions exist; mixing their
terminal values and recurrence factors would change the computation.

> Preserve the original illustrative stream

The original two-state model names its states Healthy and Fever and its three
symbols normal, cold and dizzy. These are labels in a synthetic example, with fixed
parameters supplied by the native fixture. The short sequence normal,cold,dizzy,dizzy
has sixteen hidden paths. Its direct path sum and scaled evidence agree to numeric
precision. The fourteen-symbol stream retains every original smoothed state1 value,
Viterbi state and log-likelihood. The extra filtering column shows which changes
come from future observations.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/forward_backward_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/forward_backward.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <print>
#include <limits>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto h=dm::algorithms::forward_backward_example_model();const auto obs=dm::algorithms::forward_backward_example_observations();const auto short_result=dm::algorithms::forward_backward(h,{0,1,2,2});const auto short_sum=dm::algorithms::hmm_enumerate_paths(h,{0,1,2,2});const auto r=dm::algorithms::forward_backward(h,obs);const auto v=dm::algorithms::viterbi(h,obs);
  std::print("Original short sequence: scaled evidence {:.7f}; native path sum {:.7f}; log evidence {:.5f}; paths {}.\n",std::exp(short_result.log_likelihood),short_sum.probability,short_result.log_likelihood,short_sum.paths);
  std::print("| day | symbol | filtered P(Fever) | smoothed P(Fever) | Viterbi state |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
  const std::vector<std::string> symbols{"normal","cold","dizzy"},states{"Healthy","Fever"};std::vector<double> days,filtered,smoothed,hard;
  for(std::size_t t=0;t<obs.size();++t){std::print("| {} | {} | {:.7f} | {:.7f} | {} |\n",t+1,symbols[obs[t]],r.alpha[t][1],r.gamma[t][1],states[v.states[t]]);days.push_back(double(t+1));filtered.push_back(r.alpha[t][1]);smoothed.push_back(r.gamma[t][1]);hard.push_back(double(v.states[t]));}
  std::print("\nOriginal fourteen-step log evidence {:.4f}; forward-backward product terms {}.\n",r.log_likelihood,dm::algorithms::forward_backward_work(h,obs).work.forward_transition_terms);
  auto future=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();future.lines(days,filtered,"Filtered",{37,99,235},2).points(days,filtered,"",{37,99,235},3).lines(days,smoothed,"Smoothed",{220,38,38},2).points(days,smoothed,"",{220,38,38},3).legend({"Prefix only","Whole stream"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}}).title("Filtering versus smoothing").xlab("Day, one based").ylab("Conditional probability of state Fever");
  auto decode=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();decode.lines(days,smoothed,"Smoothed",{220,38,38},2).lines(days,hard,"Viterbi",{37,99,235},1.5).abline_h(.5,{148,163,184},1).legend({"Smoothed marginal","Viterbi state0/1"},{{220,38,38},{37,99,235}}).title("A marginal versus one joint path").xlab("Day, one based").ylab("Probability or decoded state indicator");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(future).add(decode).size(1100,540).title("Original fixed model and fourteen-symbol stream").fit_panels().save_svg("build/forward_backward_original.svg");
  if(std::abs(std::exp(short_result.log_likelihood)-short_sum.probability)>1e-15L)throw std::runtime_error("original likelihood control");
}
