| observations | log evidence | exp(log evidence), double | last scale | last marginal |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1 | -0.693147 | 0.5 | 2 | 1 |
| 10 | -6.931472 | 0.000976562 | 2 | 1 |
| 100 | -69.314718 | 7.88861e-31 | 2 | 1 |
| 1000 | -693.147181 | 9.33264e-302 | 2 | 1 |
| 10000 | -6931.471806 | 0 | 2 | 1 |

Impossible sequence: negative-infinite log evidence true; gamma placeholders [0, 0]. Tiny reciprocal overflow rejected true; positive-support underflow rejected true.
\image(figures/forward_backward_numerics.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The scaled log evidence remains finite for this ten-thousand-observation control, while its double exponential is zero. Separate executed controls distinguish impossible evidence, reciprocal overflow and lost positive support.)
\alttext(A native linear plot shows negative log evidence versus sequence length for a one-state fair-symbol model, ending near6931.47 at ten thousand observations.)

Impossible evidence is a mathematical zero: no positive-weight state path explains
the sequence, so its log-likelihood is negative infinity and conditioning on it has
no posterior distribution. The returned zero gamma rows are placeholders for an undefined posterior. They must not be read as certain absence of every state.
The old implementation incorrectly retained a finite prefix log score in this case;
the canonical function now reports the impossible sequence correctly.

A different case has positive support but an actual predictive sum rounds to zero.
A Boolean support probe distinguishes that numeric failure from impossibility and
throws an underflow error. Nonfinite reciprocal scales, accumulators or updates
throw overflow errors. Smaller individual terms may still round away, so these
checks do not establish arbitrary precision or accuracy for all rare states.
Scaling does not promise to work unchanged for sequences of any length: table
capacity, memory, summation error and representable intermediate values still matter.
The widened enumerator also checks its positive prefix products for underflow;
it is a small-model reference rather than an unlimited-precision oracle.

> Actual work, admission and ownership

With N states, M symbols and T positive observations, the two recursions each
visit (T−1)*N² transition terms. A forward term has one multiplication before its
accumulation; a backward term has two. Initialization, scaling and gamma formation
add O(TN). Full model validation adds O(N²+NM), including when T=0, and observation
validation adds O(T). Total time is O(N²+NM+T+TN²); owned arrays use O(TN+T).
The ordinary result already stores actual alpha, beta, gamma and scale tables, so
no replay or redundant full-history interface is needed.

The next fixed-two-state control compares actual transition terms from both passes
with the checked count2^T of paths an enumerator would visit. The large reference
counts are forecasts, not executed enumerations or elapsed-time measurements.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/forward_backward_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/forward_backward.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <print>
#include <limits>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto h=dm::algorithms::forward_backward_example_model();std::vector<double>x,terms,paths;std::vector<std::string>labels;
  std::print("| observations | forward terms | backward terms | enumeration path forecast |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t T:{2u,4u,8u,16u,32u}){const auto w=dm::algorithms::forward_backward_work(h,std::vector<std::size_t>(T,0)).work;const auto count=dm::algorithms::hmm_enumeration_paths(h.num_states(),T);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",T,w.forward_transition_terms,w.backward_transition_terms,count);x.push_back(double(x.size()));terms.push_back(std::log2(double(w.forward_transition_terms+w.backward_transition_terms)));paths.push_back(std::log2(double(count)));labels.push_back(std::to_string(T));}
  const auto bound=dm::algorithms::forward_backward_entries(2,2);bool quota=false,domain=false,enum_cap=false,huge=false;try{dm::algorithms::forward_backward_work(h,{0,1},bound-1);}catch(const std::length_error&){quota=true;}
  auto bad=h;bad.emission.back().clear();try{dm::algorithms::forward_backward_work(bad,{0,1},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){domain=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::hmm_enumerate_paths(h,{0,1,2,2},15);}catch(const std::length_error&){enum_cap=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::hmm_enumeration_paths(2,std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max());}catch(const std::length_error&){huge=true;}
  std::vector<std::size_t>obs{0,1};const auto result=dm::algorithms::forward_backward_work(h,obs,bound);const double before=result.result.gamma[0][1];h.initial={1,0};obs[0]=2;const bool owned=result.result.gamma[0][1]==before;
  std::print("\nWhole inference entries {}; one below rejected {}; exact bound forward rows {}; original fourteen-step entries {}.\n",bound,quota,result.result.alpha.size(),dm::algorithms::forward_backward_entries(2,14));
  std::print("Checked controls: ragged model before quota {}; sixteen-path enumeration cap15 rejected {}; virtual path-count overflow {}; owned result after caller edits {}.\n",domain,enum_cap,huge,owned);
  std::print("Empty model and sequence: inference entries {}; enumeration paths {}; log evidence {:.0f}.\n",dm::algorithms::forward_backward_entries(0,0),dm::algorithms::hmm_enumeration_paths(0,0),dm::algorithms::forward_backward({},{}).log_likelihood);
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,terms,"Both recursion passes",{37,99,235},2).points(x,terms,"",{37,99,235},4).lines(x,paths,"Enumeration forecast",{220,38,38},2).points(x,paths,"",{220,38,38},4).x_tick_labels(labels).legend({"Actual transition terms","Forecast hidden paths"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}}).title("Fixed N=2: actual recursion visits versus path forecast").xlab("Observations T; consecutive powers of two").ylab("log2 of count; different operation units").size(1000,520).save_svg("build/forward_backward_work.svg");
  if(!quota||!domain||!enum_cap||!huge||!owned)throw std::runtime_error("validated admission and ownership");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
