\image(figures/forward_backward_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The blue series counts actual pair terms in both recursion passes; the red series forecasts whole hidden paths. Units differ, and neither curve measures runtime. The log2 axis keeps the exponential reference visible.)
\alttext(A native line plot compares log-base-two actual transition-term counts with log-base-two hidden-path forecasts for two states and sequence lengths two, four, eight, sixteen and thirty-two.)

All shapes are checked before probability values. Initial probabilities, every
transition row and every emission row must have finite entries in[0,1] summing to
one within absolute1e−12 in widened arithmetic. There must be N transition rows of
length N and N equal, nonempty emission rows. Parameters are never silently
normalized. Observations and supplied state-path IDs are zero based and validated
in full before indexing. The entirely empty model with empty observations has
likelihood one, log-likelihood zero and empty inference tables. Invalid models are
still rejected for empty observations.

For N,T>0 the work API admits the whole result using C=4T+3TN entry records:
three row records and one scale value per time, plus three N-scalar rows. The
bound is zero if either dimension is zero. These are entries, not bytes or peak
RAM; container objects and exceptional support scratch are additional. The default
cap is one million entries; zero disables only the optional cap and retains all
representability checks. The historical two-argument function has no optional cap.
Both paths share the executing kernel, and every returned table owns its storage.
Full validation happens before admission, allocation or empty shortcuts. Failures
return no partial result and leave caller parameters and observations untouched.

Enumeration has a separate default cap of one million paths, with zero disabling
only that cap. Checked integer N^T and T*N^T bounds remain; there is no floating
pow-to-integer conversion. Its time is O(T*N^T) after model validation, with O(TN+T)
output and O(T) path scratch. Empty observations enumerate one empty path of mass
one. A strict best-weight comparison keeps the first enumerated tie; that tie
policy need not match Viterbi's predecessor policy.

The fixed illustrative models require no external dataset. All figures are native
C++ outputs saved locally, and the complete programs above are their editable sources.
